SON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string. The Python source must define solve(case). Must not mutate case. Use only standard library.\n\nWe'll write code accordingly.\n\nLet's produce the code string. Use triple quotes? But inside JSON string, we need to escape double quotes and newlines. We'll write Python code with proper indentation, then encode as JSON string.\n\nI'll write the code:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    # extract fields\n    round_scores = case['round_scores']\n    round_targets = case['round_targets']\n    forced = case['forced']\n    # number of tokens\n    num_tokens = len(round_scores[0])\n    # initially all indices active\n    active = list(range(num_tokens))\n    history = []\n    # validate: forced indices must be within range\n    for f in forced:\n        assert 0 <= f < num_tokens, \"Forced index out of range\"\n    for i, scores in enumerate(round_scores):\n        target = round_targets[i]\n        # separate forced indices that are still active\n        forced_in_active = [idx for idx in forced if idx in active]\n        # ensure target >= number of forced\n        if target < len(forced_in_active):\n            # infeasible; perhaps raise or return something? but contract says reject infeasible targets.\n            # We'll raise a ValueError\n            raise ValueError(\"Infeasible target: forced more than target\")\n        # remaining positions to fill from non-forced active\n        non_forced = [idx for idx in active if idx not in forced_in_active]\n        # sort non_forced by scores descending\n        non_forced_sorted = sorted(non_forced, key=lambda idx: scores[idx], reverse=True)\n        # select top (target - len(forced_in_active))\n        selected_non_forced = non_forced_sorted[:target - len(forced_in_active)]\n        # combine forced and selected, then sort by index to preserve original order\n        retained = sorted(forced_in_active + selected_non_forced)\n        # update